# Offline recovery model

54 cases: 51 injected faults and 3 successful paths. Assertions: true.

## Assumptions
- One serialized writer; each modeled write mutates one field atomically.
- Every applied write survives simulated reload, in program order; no torn writes.
- An exception may occur before or after a mutation; all exceptions stop forward execution.
- Raw registry is an opaque UTF-8 string, never parsed/sanitized; missing is explicit null.
- All participating routes honor journal quarantine; reload never retries effects automatically.
- The modeled item backup is abstract, not proof of complete ItemStack serialization.

## Limits
- No Bedrock transaction, fsync, persistence ordering or engine-event guarantee is established.
- Preserved evidence is not restored gameplay state, availability, or exactly-once delivery.
- A journal ignored by an older pack cannot enforce quarantine after downgrade.
- No event generation token means a late old event and a valid new event can be indistinguishable.
- Completed journal entries also block further modeled operations: no liveness, tombstone GC or reuse policy is proved.
- Generation is an abstract label only; it is not supplied by native events or proved globally unique.
- No integrated protocol, repair command, migration, world access, pack change or publication.

Counterexamples and per-step traces are in report.json. Run: node --test tools/recovery-analysis.node-test.mjs && node tools/recovery-analysis.mjs.
